          "status": "supported"
        }
      },
      "B": {
        "reading_checked": "If the axes accurately encode comparable regional values, labels attach to their adjacent markers, the displayed top regions are sufficiently representative of regions beyond A–E, and association is accepted as sufficient decision evidence rather than proof of advertising causality, then a consistent positive association supports approving a broader ad spend increase.",
